  release-candidate-review: the charter for the orchestrated review
    wave before declaring a release candidate for serious human
    review (VD 2026-08-16), targeting the two defect families the
    per-slice gate structure cannot see
    (docs/plans/release-candidate-review.md). The second whole-branch
    review's calibration lane found 8 BLOCKERS/44 MAJORS/35 MINORS
    confirmed (docs/plans/review-2026-08-24/consolidated-report.md).
    Family 1, correctness
    beyond the gates' reach - the slice batteries prove diffs neutral
    against agent-recorded baselines, never that the baselines were
    right. Seed classes: math-vs-history oracles (exact-posterior and
    Geweke-style joint checks, deeper SBC per family - the
    sbc-family-tiers machinery exists); test-suite strength
    (vacuous-assertion audit, package-scale sampled mutation,
    coverage of never-executed branches); whole-surface coherence
    once the surface is frozen (naming, defaults, Rd-vs-behavior,
    examples, plan-vs-landed audit); a fresh adversarial whole-branch
    review; the consumer-bundle re-run plus .win-variant drift; and
    the analysis legs this host cannot run (rchk/valgrind workflows
    exist but bind to the default branch - see the release section
    below; TSAN/gctorture have no leg anywhere). Family 2,
    accumulation - agent-written slices breed edit-history sediment,
    missed factorization across the five fitting surfaces, surface
    and feature inconsistency, dialect drift, and over-complication.
    Seed review kinds: sediment (blame-informed hunt for code whose
    justification names a state that no longer exists); factorization
    (semantic duplication, with docs/design the arbiter of
    INTENTIONAL divergence); justify-this-element simplicity; style
    normalization. Findings land as behavior-neutral cleanup slices
    under the standard bitwise battery - cheap only while the
    no-compat window is open. The seed lists are a floor, not a
    bound: this item's orchestrator re-derives the slate first and is
    expected to find classes this entry overlooks. Load-bearing
    ordering only: run after bart2-argument-consolidation closes;
    land accumulation cleanups BEFORE the coverage/mutation/coherence
    passes (reshaping invalidates them); behavior-level oracles may
    run in parallel with anything. RC declaration itself stays
    VD-held.
